{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "054B", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-constructible-quasi-compact-quasi-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9651110046b3737a3aaba5f8ec6e85e5c672b54bb1c97d235ddf35facbbc4cf3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a1a670d7c75416b6fdae68a5eab416cc7053d50ed51f36126edb5913c0fea07d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme.\nAny locally constructible subset of <MATH_0002> is constructible.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ef64b2d6e0024724315fa2172a6da5d059c71eebea8a564ae7d26fdf0c37ebe8", "unit_id": "tag:054E:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "054B", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X = V_1 \\cup \\ldots \\cup V_m$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$V_i$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$E \\subset X$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$E \\cap V_j$", "MATH_0009": "$V_j$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-separated-quasi-compact-open-retrocompact}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topology-lemma-collate-constructible}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-locally-constructible}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e43ea25f27b2a9d9facaadf35b9cbe4e815b93e1a02188d3cef5b9b1f0f8ab66", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:25824c86dd097364abfb04bc1815483a42569b316895f0166f0b4c60b571dfb8", "source_text": "As <MATH_0001> is quasi-compact we can choose a finite affine open covering\n<MATH_0002>. As <MATH_0003> is quasi-separated each <MATH_0004> is\nretrocompact in <MATH_0005> by\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nHence by\nTopology, Lemma <REF_0002>\nwe see that <MATH_0006> is constructible in <MATH_0007> if and only if\n<MATH_0008> is constructible in <MATH_0009>. Thus we win by\nLemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3f16a36973b314e330c91329d491dcd4af5c72e7d538215764ec137cac75569a", "unit_id": "tag:054E:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "054B", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$E$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$E \\cap U$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-retrocompact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:72a266b1bb2a50d7d49b05cf671056a6741c067b5e575c630762fb77f44aa53b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ae42dc960e0348c41bc074ef0ea4eb2caf77fe81b2da55944240e482c116795e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. A subset <MATH_0002> of <MATH_0003> is retrocompact in <MATH_0004> if and only if\n<MATH_0005> is quasi-compact for every affine open <MATH_0006> of <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:81eaba48a6fb55dbb1ae64fcd340c05320610eeaa85904dd199edd89d8e9844c", "unit_id": "tag:07ZL:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "054B", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d2cdd54c91172842da7935e351b2e537dfc65808da525fec53dd82898c278104", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6fe4973dbd92e2fc4e20a614c20502409a602459a33a252874dbdbbc7b8f0357", "source_text": "Immediate from the fact that every quasi-compact open of <MATH_0001> is a finite\nunion of affine opens.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6b4deec1381e82071bf2b81da0475d2b65037641c399846ee96b0370e9183819", "unit_id": "tag:07ZL:proof"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "054B", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X = \\coprod_{i \\in I} X_i$", "MATH_0002": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-stratification-locally-finite-constructible}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ec7e2e49cbaf2f8621dcc3ed0c1fbc5c44c38f2eec1be8c9cf4b0c27000581a1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f018065cce7100a22552048f0fa21a6fdecfe9e715f1d90b8b5980d3d5525087", "source_text": "A partition <MATH_0001> of a scheme <MATH_0002> with\nretrocompact parts is locally finite if and only if the parts\nare locally constructible.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9d675e48516d8e5b92ebaa783c7075c05febc66ce223f710d7299946692dd3e8", "unit_id": "tag:0F2M:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "054B", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0002": "$U = \\coprod_{i \\in I} U \\cap X_i$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\cap X_i$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\cap X_i$", "MATH_0006": "$X_i$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0008": "$U = \\coprod X_i \\cap U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-definition-quasi-compact}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topology-definition-paritition}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{topology-definition-locally-finite}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{topology-lemma-locally-closed-constructible-image}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-locally-constructible}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{topology-lemma-constructible-hausdorff-quasi-compact}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0ae5e4fd3c61bfdfede1b1d54e5f6ae5a8b8eefe1ed528d0e05991bf75b7d053", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:49747fdeab0f67234930306b982f0bc941ac5a8d6c228ed0d531186c619077c9", "source_text": "See Topology, Definitions\n<REF_0001>,\n<REF_0002>, and\n<REF_0003>\nfor the definitions of retrocompact, partition, and locally finite.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nIf the partition is locally finite and <MATH_0001> is an\naffine open, then we see that <MATH_0002>\nis a finite partition (more precisely, all but a finite number\nof its parts are empty). Hence <MATH_0003> is quasi-compact\nand its complement is retrocompact in <MATH_0004> as a finite union\nof retrocompact parts. Thus <MATH_0005> is constructible\nby Topology, Lemma <REF_0004>.\nIt follows that <MATH_0006> is locally constructible by\nLemma <REF_0005>.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nAssume the parts are locally constructible. Then for any affine\nopen <MATH_0007> we obtain a covering <MATH_0008>\nby constructible subsets. Since the constructible topology is\nquasi-compact, see\nTopology, Lemma <REF_0006>,\nthis covering has a finite refinement, i.e.,\nthe partition is locally finite.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a892199d50ac71e4dad9addfe0843d23de4b86bba1fbfcfa65f2755da1afebd6", "unit_id": "tag:0F2M:proof"}
